OPI: Yes, this request is seeking records from ADM(Materiel) / the CPSP project office, as the Defence Investment
 Agency operates under ADM(Materiel) and holds all CPSP project evaluation, ITB scoring, and procurement governance records.

Timeframe: I am maintaining the original timeframe of January
 1, 2024 to April 11, 2026 (inclusive). Canada's Fighting Against Forced Labour and Child Labour in Supply Chains Act (S.C.
 2023, c. 9) came into force on January 1, 2024, and any supply chain compliance assessments of Hanwha Ocean's facilities or proposed ITB partners initiated under that Act begin from that date. Early-stage DIA assessments of Hanwha Ocean's proposed university
 and industry partner ecosystem also predate the formal 2025 RFP stage. Narrowing to January 1, 2025 would exclude records generated during the Act's initial compliance period and the ITB framework planning phase.

Record versions: I do not consent to a limitation to final versions only. Please include all responsive records
 regardless of draft status — including working documents, email chains, routing notes, and intermediate assessments — subject to applicable exemptions and severance under s. 25 of the Access to Information
 Act.

Keywords: I confirm that the keywords are used in the context of the CPSP program and are not intended as standalone
 search terms, consistent with your suggestion.

Rescope structure: The eight-item structure in your rescope suggestion accurately reflects the intent of the
 original request. I consent to the rewording you proposed for items 1 through 8, subject to the timeframe and draft-version corrections stated above.

Please proceed with processing on this basis.

Thank you for your assistance.

